{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan","id":1445137,"title":"Im going to play my first session, and i need help choosing a clan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-21T15:12:07-07:00","id":1445137,"title":"Im going to play my first session, and i need help choosing a clan","content":"So my friend is hosting a session for me and other friends of his.<br /> so since this is my first character i wanted to do a little self insert.<br /> the character i have in mind is a loner nerd, he knows stuff about forums and some basic computer stuff nothing more.<br /> also he read some books about anarchism and he sees it as the right thing, he believes that there can be no justice or equality if you dont bring the fight to the ones opressing people, he is not your typical sjw, he is kinda of a mix between an incel and a leftist.<br /> and even tho he likes being alone, something he always wanted in his life was camaraderie, someone he could trust, no tricks etc, someone who he would have their back and they would have his.<br /> <br /> so to all you veterans out there which clan do you think this dude would fit in?<br /> <br /> anyway, thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> oh i forgot to add i think its going to be v5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","user":"Abesolus","date":". 04-21-2021, 06:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:22:18-07:00","id":1445140,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu. Nosferatu. Nosferatu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T15:38:31-07:00","id":1445144,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu is kind of the go-to clan for nerdy incel computer guy, but really any clan can be. What role do you see yourself performing in the group? Are you the guy who negotiates? Pick any of the Presence clans. Are you the front-line fighter? Gangrel or Brujah. Are you an assassin? Pick any of the Obfuscate clans. Do you want to be the group wizard, either literally or metaphorically? Pick any of the Auspex or Thaumaturgy clans.<br /> <br /> What is your favorite vampire movie? Pick a clan whose Discipline are similar to that vampire. <br /> <br /> What is your favorite fantasy type unrelated to vampires? Gangrel and Brujah can be specced similar to Barbarians. Any of the Presence clans can be specced similar to Bards. The Thaumaturgy clans are, of course, Wizards. Any of the Obfuscate clans can be Rogues. Gangrel can be Druids, as can certain Tremere, depending on what element of Druids you like best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T16:17:22-07:00","id":1445151,"title":"","content":"Anarchist looking for Comraderie honestly bars most of them. Do you like animals? Gangrel fair pretty well in V5. Tzmisce sound good. Hecata if you wanna get weird? Honestly, if you don't mind being cursed with ugly, Nosferatu is really the option that ticks the most boxes for you. You want clans that don't have Presence (Though it's very strong in this edition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T16:25:24-07:00","id":1445155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445151#post1445151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anarchist looking for Comraderie honestly bars most of them. Do you like animals? Gangrel fair pretty well in V5. Tzmisce sound good. Hecata if you wanna get weird? Honestly, if you don't mind being cursed with ugly, Nosferatu is really the option that ticks the most boxes for you. You want clans that don't have Presence (Though it's very strong in this edition)</div> </div> </div> </div>its not like i hate animals, but dogs really get under my skin, barking all the time ugh, and obfuscate is my favorite discipline. only thing that bothers me is being deformed.... but whatever. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T17:55:01-07:00","id":1445163,"title":"","content":"People have already mentioned Brujah, but I just wanted to mention them as a good fit for lefty anarchist political leanings. Less for nerdy loners, but playing an exception to stereotypes can be fun, just need to understand what motivated the sire's &quot;unusual&quot; choice. The Anarchs getting more into tech provides that.<br /> <br /> Also, the idea of a gamer freaking out becomes downright hilarious when you add Brujah rage on top.<br /> <br /> My other recommendation, one of the Clans that hooked my interest recently, would be Malkavian. Auspex and Obfuscate both fit well for someone who keeps hidden and likes to observe from a distance (aka through a computer screen).<br /> <br /> The tricky part with a Malk is their Clan Flaw. Dunno how much it may have changed in V5, but picking a flavour of crazy that is both interesting but not being too much of a nuisance for the rest of the coterie can be a balancing act.<br /> <br /> One possible idea/example? Your Malk doesn't just like computers, they now think they're *alive,* with thoughts and feelings and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:07:10-07:00","id":1445166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445163#post1445163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the idea of a gamer freaking out becomes downright hilarious when you add Brujah rage on top.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Heh! Yeah, that was my first thought when he said he liked computers and the Anarchists: a Brujah smashing his computer because someone trolled him online. :-p<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T18:16:47-07:00","id":1445168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445166#post1445166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh! Yeah, that was my first thought when he said he liked computers and the Anarchists: a Brujah smashing his computer because someone trolled him online. :-p</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Brujah might start Skyping for all their meetings; a new computer is probably easier than possibly sending another Brujah into torpor or Final Death due to frenzy lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:47:10-07:00","id":1445189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445166#post1445166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh! Yeah, that was my first thought when he said he liked computers and the Anarchists: a Brujah smashing his computer because someone trolled him online. :-p</div> </div> </div> </div>your thoughts on gangrel? i kinda like them being loners but im not into animals lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:53:28-07:00","id":1445190,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel and the Tzim are my favorite clans, as I like sending swarms of animals to skin my enemies alive. But if you don't like animals, Gangrel still have Protean and Fortitude. Just maxing those takes a very long time, especially if you are also buying skills and loresheets and so forth. And you could always develop some out-of-clan Disciplines if you find you still have XP to burn after maxing Prot and Fort. That's a hella long campaign if you have all of that XP.<br /> <br /> Also, your ST might allow you to play a City Gangrel that defected to the Anarchs/Cammies or had a sire who did. Boom, you've got Obfuscate, Celerity, and Protean, and your loner concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T19:56:19-07:00","id":1445192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abesolus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445189#post1445189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">your thoughts on gangrel? i kinda like them being loners but im not into animals lol</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can do pretty much whatever you want, so long as you can think of a good story for it. But a Gangrel seems an odd choice IMO. Even City Gangrel are more &quot;street&quot; than &quot;basement dweller.&quot; Unless you're really into Protean, seems like other choices may be better.<br /> <br /> Edit: I didn't know or totally forgot that City Gangrel trade Animalism for Obfuscate :O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:05:31-07:00","id":1445193,"title":"","content":"so ive come up with 2 characters<br /> <br /> the antisocial brujah nerd, he doesnt like to hang out much but hes up to kick some rich fucks ass with the crew when needed.<br /> vs<br /> the antisocial basement dweller nosferatu, he aint that good at reading or talking to people but he can find stuff online, and he is eager to learn.<br /> <br /> i know both need more work but its something to start at least, which sounds better?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:09:49-07:00","id":1445196,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;better&quot;. It's a game. Better is whatever you would enjoy more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:15:57-07:00","id":1445197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445196#post1445196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Define &quot;better&quot;. It's a game. Better is whatever you would enjoy more.</div> </div> </div> </div>by better i meant it doesnt sound childish or like a <span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Gary Stu, something that fits within the world of darkness.<br /> also, my word choice always sucked, sorry.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:21:29-07:00","id":1445200,"title":"","content":"I'm going to suggest Malk or Tremere. They don't have any of those.. unnerdy physical discplines. They have Superior senses which let you read people and access hidden bits on the internet.(I've never really understood why Nos get a pass at being the internet clan.. they have no real aptitudes for it.) Malk's let you hide(WHich you would also get as a Nos.. so you're at this point just SLIGHTLY BETTER Than them at doing any social networking...) Both have Mind control which.. is pretty much the best trick for hacking.<br /> <br /> Tremere get blood magic which has been signficantly nerfed By not having a couple hundred secondary paths BUT it does still have rituals which is the bread and butter of one off weird powers. So its still the most versitile discipline in the book even if its not &quot;More versitile than every other power that exists&quot; Between House Ipissmus and carna you aren't stuck in vampire facist land.. well any more than any other vampire is. Of course.. this still makes Tremere a harder style to play. If you want an easy go at it be the crazy internet guy and go Malkavian. If you want to be the Quadratic Mage even after nerfs of v5.. its Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:24:32-07:00","id":1445201,"title":"","content":"They both sound fine. Really, being a Gary Stu in these games is, in my experience, less about basic concepts and more about whether you are willing to roleplay weaknesses and accept bad things happening to your character without bitching out the ST. I've seen people with completely reasonable concepts lose their shit because the ST gave them a stain. And I've seen people with concepts that sounded like they snuck something crazy past the ST on character creation actually be wonderful players because they were fully committed to roleplaying the weaknesses and complications inherent in their out-there concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T20:33:36-07:00","id":1445204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445200#post1445200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I've never really understood why Nos get a pass at being the internet clan.. they have no real aptitudes for it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about aptitudes, it's about them being the only clan that has managed to make information-socialism work. As individuals, Nos are indeed inferior to both Malks and Tremere at information gathering, but as a clan, Nos win this. Nosferatu freely give each other information, with the understanding that while Nos A may not profit from information he gives to Nos B, one day Nos B will freely give information to Nos A, and Nos A will profit then.<br /> <br /> That's not something that happens with the Tremere, who hoard secrets as they attempt to climb over each other reaching for the top of the pyramid.<br /> <br /> Malks are likely as not to confuse the information they gathered with the voices in their heads, and may not be able to communicate it in a clear and concise manner.<br /> <br /> Socialism, even a clan-specific information-socialism, is inconceivable for the other clans. Nosferatu are unique in having made it work.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T22:43:13-07:00","id":1445224,"title":"","content":"Aside from the connection with the Clan-wide information network above, my take was that the Nosferatu have often been an &quot;underdog&quot; Clan, with a weakness that significantly hinders their ability to play the social games with the kine that are the bread and butter of the more powerful Clans. They're the Clan that needs to take every advantage it can get; combined with their information culture, it makes sense that they would be the early-adopters of the Internet among the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was also a joke about basement-trolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T23:30:18-07:00","id":1445228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445204#post1445204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about aptitudes, it's about them being the only clan that has managed to make information-socialism work. As individuals, Nos are indeed inferior to both Malks and Tremere at information gathering, but as a clan, Nos win this. Nosferatu freely give each other information, with the understanding that while Nos A may not profit from information he gives to Nos B, one day Nos B will freely give information to Nos A, and Nos A will profit then.<br /> <br /> That's not something that happens with the Tremere, who hoard secrets as they attempt to climb over each other reaching for the top of the pyramid.<br /> <br /> Malks are likely as not to confuse the information they gathered with the voices in their heads, and may not be able to communicate it in a clear and concise manner.<br /> <br /> Socialism, even a clan-specific information-socialism, is inconceivable for the other clans. Nosferatu are unique in having made it work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So basically something that requires ST buy in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T09:03:50-07:00","id":1445276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445228#post1445228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically something that requires ST buy in.</div> </div> </div> </div>To go back to the ol' Nature vs. Nurture, Nossies being the Internet Clan is a Nurture thing, not a Nature thing. I'd say it's less the Storyteller and more the game developers who wrote things that way. Though a ST at home could change it for their home canon, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T11:23:39-07:00","id":1445300,"title":"","content":"I would play a Caitiff, being a clanless let you choose the disciplines you want, even being a outcast from the bottom of the pole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T13:57:31-07:00","id":1445329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445276#post1445276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To go back to the ol' Nature vs. Nurture, Nossies being the Internet Clan is a Nurture thing, not a Nature thing. I'd say it's less the Storyteller and more the game developers who wrote things that way. Though a ST at home could change it for their home canon, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you want to get a Nos who has the advantage of the situation requires the ST understanding it and and playing along with it since there's no mechanical method to push the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T14:05:44-07:00","id":1445332,"title":"","content":"I mean, ShrekNet isn't technically a *mechanic,* but I think it's a bit bigger than just a Storyteller thing, it's written into the background of the setting. You are editing or ignoring core content if the Nos have not set up the &quot;vampire Internet,&quot; and have significant control over who can access it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T20:52:26-07:00","id":1445408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445332#post1445332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, ShrekNet isn't technically a *mechanic,* but I think it's a bit bigger than just a Storyteller thing, it's written into the background of the setting. You are editing or ignoring core content if the Nos have not set up the &quot;vampire Internet,&quot; and have significant control over who can access it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its written into the background of the setting that random Anarchs can hack it, and before people start saying &quot;V5 ruined everything&quot; that was one of the few metaplot points in v20. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:21:56-07:00","id":1445417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445408#post1445408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its written into the background of the setting that random Anarchs can hack it, and before people start saying &quot;V5 ruined everything&quot; that was one of the few metaplot points in v20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, but the Nosferatu built it.<br /> <br /> It's less that the Nosferatu are THE Internet Clan and more that they are The Internet Clan. Plenty of other Kindred do wild stuff with technology, including the Internet, but the Nosferatu got there first, and more collectively. It is reductive to act like they are the ONLY tech-proficient Clan. See my recommendation for a Malkavian <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:44:10-07:00","id":1445421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445417#post1445417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh yeah, but the Nosferatu built it.<br /> <br /> It's less that the Nosferatu are THE Internet Clan and more that they are The Internet Clan. Plenty of other Kindred do wild stuff with technology, including the Internet, but the Nosferatu got there first, and more collectively. It is reductive to act like they are the ONLY tech-proficient Clan. See my recommendation for a Malkavian <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>the Nos claimed to make an unhackable internet for the Camarilla.. and failed.<br /> <br /> The Assamites uploaded their entire magical library to a CD rom and handed out copies.<br /> <br /> A small Group of radical anarch tremere developed the ability to EMAIL you Discplines. Like full on Matrix &quot;I know Kung fu&quot; but.. Potence.<br /> <br /> I'd argue rather the Nos got there first and while no one else was putting in any effort they were. Now people have and they don't really matter as much. They have lost what advantage they had.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T21:52:23-07:00","id":1445424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445421#post1445421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Nos claimed to make an unhackable internet for the Camarilla.. and failed.<br /> <br /> The Assamites uploaded their entire magical library to a CD rom and handed out copies.<br /> <br /> A small Group of radical anarch tremere developed the ability to EMAIL you Discplines. Like full on Matrix &quot;I know Kung fu&quot; but.. Potence.<br /> <br /> I'd argue rather the Nos got there first and while no one else was putting in any effort they were. Now people have and they don't really matter as much. They have lost what advantage they had.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we seem to mostly agree.<br /> <br /> I haven't read the V20 books covering the details of how far other Kindred have developed their abilities with the Internet. I just know that the Nos probably got their Internet Clan rep from setting up Shreknet, which I noted was because their situation makes them likely &quot;early adopters,&quot; not any innate attributes they possess. Reputations take time to die, and the Nos made a reputation with Shreknet. I'm not defending it as perfect, just notable enough and early enough to explain the reputation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T04:08:02-07:00","id":1445457,"title":"","content":"I don't say Nosferatu because computers; sure, they like computers, but near everyone these days under 40 likes computers and it's not like the other clans are going to go &quot;oh he likes computers, better give him to the nos&quot;. Unless you're at the stage of actually coding proficiently, you're not special for liking computers. (if anything, the fact that half of them haven't actively tried to recruit more computer experts to counter the nosferatu is a little puzzling. The Tremere and Ventrue seem to be the only other clans with an active interest)<br /> <br /> It's the leftist incel part, and the part where Nosferatu genuinely cooperate a lot better with one another due to their shared weakness in comparison to other clans that makes me go &quot;nosferatu, Nosferatu, Nosferatu. They're the Clan that's a family (a very ugly family, but a family) It's also a family that'll support you even if you want to be an &quot;anarchist&quot; (just don't go providing false information and damage the clan's fame for integrity.)<br /> <br /> only downside is that obfuscate and potence got tanked in the new edition, making it difficult to pull off the shenanigans I'm used to (unless you're an elder)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T10:02:56-07:00","id":1445681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445200#post1445200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to suggest Malk or Tremere. They don't have any of those.. unnerdy physical discplines. They have Superior senses which let you read people and access hidden bits on the internet.(I've never really understood why Nos get a pass at being the internet clan.. they have no real aptitudes for it.) Malk's let you hide(WHich you would also get as a Nos.. so you're at this point just SLIGHTLY BETTER Than them at doing any social networking...) Both have Mind control which.. is pretty much the best trick for hacking.<br /> <br /> Tremere get blood magic which has been signficantly nerfed By not having a couple hundred secondary paths BUT it does still have rituals which is the bread and butter of one off weird powers. So its still the most versitile discipline in the book even if its not &quot;More versitile than every other power that exists&quot; Between House Ipissmus and carna you aren't stuck in vampire facist land.. well any more than any other vampire is. Of course.. this still makes Tremere a harder style to play. If you want an easy go at it be the crazy internet guy and go Malkavian. If you want to be the Quadratic Mage even after nerfs of v5.. its Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> arent malkavians crazy and dont care about self preservation? i kinda like the clan (since i have a mental health problem) but yeah if they dont care about their life i think its too much for me, lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T10:13:46-07:00","id":1445683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Abesolus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445681#post1445681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> arent malkavians crazy and dont care about self preservation? i kinda like the clan (since i have a mental health problem) but yeah if they dont care about their life i think its too much for me, lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Malkavians are supernaturally insane, every single one of them. But that's not the same as suicidal or incapable of taking care of one's self. Those Malkavians DO exist, but they're generally locked up by the rest of the Clan, or other Vampires occasionally. Player character Malkavians are generally assumed to be the functional sort, and some Malkavians are extremely lucid with their Derangement Clan Flaw being one particular trait that is just *off*. <br /> <br /> I'm blanking on his name, but Beckett's Jyhad Diary featured a Malkavian Prince who was extremely functional; his derangement was basically kind of like a reverse-Truman-show, where he thinks everything going on around him is just a &quot;show&quot; or &quot;movie.&quot; There was an anecdote referring to a significant setback that might have driven another Prince into frenzy, but he just kinda sighed and said &quot;No point getting so invested in such a crappy show.&quot; It doesn't seem to stop him from mostly taking things serious enough to be regarded as doing a good job generally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:16:17-07:00","id":1445691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445683#post1445683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Malkavians are supernaturally insane, every single one of them. But that's not the same as suicidal or incapable of taking care of one's self. Those Malkavians DO exist, but they're generally locked up by the rest of the Clan, or other Vampires occasionally. Player character Malkavians are generally assumed to be the functional sort, and some Malkavians are extremely lucid with their Derangement Clan Flaw being one particular trait that is just *off*</div> </div> </div> </div>Two of my all time favorites are Dr. Netchurch (and the Detached Scientist template he's derived from; especially the time he &quot;logically talked&quot; someone into killing himself &quot;for the greater good&quot;, apparently either unaware of or repressing that he'd obviously used Dominate to do it), and the EMT/Paramedic template who suffers from Sanguinary Animism (the idea that the souls of those you feed on haunt you).<br /> <br /> But &quot;embittered loner&quot; is a concept that can work with all the clans. I think at least two thirds of the original clanbooks have at least one as a template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T12:28:12-07:00","id":1445693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445691#post1445691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two of my all time favorites are Dr. Netchurch (and the Detached Scientist template he's derived from; especially the time he &quot;logically talked&quot; someone into killing himself &quot;for the greater good&quot;, apparently either unaware of or repressing that he'd obviously used Dominate to do it), and the EMT/Paramedic template who suffers from Sanguinary Animism (the idea that the souls of those you feed on haunt you).<br /> <br /> But &quot;embittered loner&quot; is a concept that can work with all the clans. I think at least two thirds of the original clanbooks have at least one as a template.</div> </div> </div> </div>Netchurch is an excellent example as well, since his insanity is mostly an inconvenience for the people he subconsciously Dominates into giving &quot;consent&quot; for his experiments. Or into killing themselves, hadn't heard about that gem, lol. Oh Doctor Netchurch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T13:04:31-07:00","id":1445701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445693#post1445693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Netchurch is an excellent example as well, since his insanity is mostly an inconvenience for the people he subconsciously Dominates into giving &quot;consent&quot; for his experiments. Or into killing themselves, hadn't heard about that gem, lol. Oh Doctor Netchurch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's one of those &quot;blink and you'll miss it&quot; things that comes out of left field in his narration from Ghouls: Fatal Addiction or Time of Thin Blood. He's talking about one of his subjects and just casually mentions that her father (IIRC) had killed himself after Netchurch had explained to him why it would be a good idea. And when I say casually, I mean like pass-the-salt-during-dinner level of &quot;this is an everyday totally unremarkable type thing that happens all the time&quot; nonchalant. He's either so delusional that he doesn't realize what he's done or he is so sociopathic that he doesn't care, and I not sure which is more disturbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:12:47-07:00","id":1445706,"title":"","content":"maybe im being a bit annoying and im sorry about that, last night before sleeping my mind was crafting some stuff.<br /> i love the nosferatu havens/warrens, they seem cozy and kinda make me feel at home (dark room etc)<br /> malkavian on the other hand the only thing in them that kinda reflects me is being not normal since i mostly have obsessions and between some months hear some stuff that aint there, and thats it.<br /> my friend said that nosferatu is more my thing but idk there is this lingering feeling at the back of my head still..<br /> <br /> anyway, sorry to everyone that tried to help me, im dumb as a brick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26805-abesolus","name":"Abesolus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:20:51-07:00","id":1445707,"title":"","content":"Go Caitiff, problem solved","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T14:40:35-07:00","id":1445712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445137-im-going-to-play-my-first-session-and-i-need-help-choosing-a-clan?p=1445707#post1445707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go Caitiff, problem solved</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually was considering Caitiff as well. If you're not interested in dealing with/working around the particular flaws or stereotypes of a given Clan, a Caitiff is a good option. But I dunno how much the rules for them might have changed in V5; I'd say that being able to pick your favourite &quot;vampire weakness&quot; from pop culture as a Flaw can really let you tune your personal Vampire to your preference, but I'm not sure Flaws are still a thing, or work the same way.<br /> <br /> PS Being indecisive isn't &quot;dumb,&quot; especially when you're still figuring things out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> To the extent that you're looking to make a &quot;self-insert&quot; character explicitly, I would say that you and your friends probably know better than us what &quot;fits.&quot; But really, the most important thing is to have fun, so unless you're really committed to the closest match with RL possible, I'd focus more on the idea you find enjoyable than the idea that is more &quot;you.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 04-24-2021, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T16:55:55-07:00","id":1445738,"title":"","content":"Brujah, Caitiff, or even Thin-Blood works honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}